# Vulnerabilities accepted after review. One CVE per line, each with a comment above it:
# why it does not affect us, who accepted it, and an expiry date. Trivy supports
# `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` after the ID; after that date the CVE fails the scan again.
#
# Example:
# # Only reachable through feature X, which we do not use. Accepted 2026-11-25.
# CVE-2026-12345 exp:2027-02-25

# Terraform state bucket uses SSE-S3 (AWS-managed keys), not a customer-managed KMS key.
# The bucket is private, HTTPS-only and versioned, and no secrets are stored in state; a KMS key
# would add access control per key and a decryption audit trail for about $1/month. Accepted by
# the repository owner on 2026-11-26 to keep Phase 0 at no cost; revisit before production state
# exists (Phase 8). See infra/bootstrap/state.tf.
AWS-0132 exp:2027-05-26
